& [GeneratedBindingFinding] is exact
  + [package] is windows-sys 0.61.2
  + [CreateFileW] returns a raw HANDLE and requires Security in the generated signature
  + [GetFileInformationByHandleEx] accepts one FILE_INFO_BY_HANDLE_CLASS, output pointer, and u32 byte size
  + [GetFinalPathNameByHandleW] accepts a WCHAR buffer, u32 character count, and flags
  + [GetVolumeInformationByHandleW] accepts two WCHAR buffers and three u32 scalar outputs
  + [FILE_ID_INFO] is u64 volume serial plus FILE_ID_128
  + [FILE_REMOTE_PROTOCOL_INFO] begins with u16 StructureVersion, u16 StructureSize, u32 Protocol, three u16 protocol-version fields, one reserved u16, and u32 Flags

& [OfficialReturnFinding] distinguishes failure from bounded-success processing
  + [GetFinalPath_success] returns string length excluding NUL
  + [GetFinalPath_small_buffer] returns required size including NUL rather than zero
  + [GetFinalPath_other_failure] returns zero and requires immediate extended-error capture
  + [GetVolumeInformation_failure] returns zero when not all requested information is retrieved and requires immediate extended-error capture
  + [consequence] a returned required size above Cantor's bound is not honestly a Win32-error result

& [TransformationFinding] is independent of API failure
  + [possible_local_fault] returned WCHARs can fail strict UTF-16 conversion
  + [possible_local_fault] returned values can violate Cantor text, structure, path, identity, or disposition form constraints
  + [possible_local_fault] returned length can exceed the fixed resource bound
  + [consequence] local transformation or semantic rejection must not be reported as an operating-system error

& [RequestFinding] is missing from profile 0.1
  + [current] every result repeats profile, target, and input root
  + [gap] no strict request type exists for validating these fields before an effect
  + [consequence] runtime code would either duplicate private root grammar or construct a fake result only to validate input

& [OwnershipFinding] supports later isolation
  + [Rust] OwnedHandle closes on drop
  + [Rust] FromRawHandle transfers close responsibility only from an open owned CloseHandle-compatible resource
  + [required_gate] INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE must be rejected before the single ownership transfer
  + [required_isolation] the current workspace unsafe_code forbid must remain intact for existing crates
  + [future_candidate] one new target-specific crate with deny-by-default unsafe and one private allow-scoped seam

& [LintProbe] is local and non-authoritative
  + [result] rustc 1.96 accepts an allow-scoped private module under crate-level deny unsafe_code
  + [boundary] this proves lint mechanics only and authorizes no production unsafe code

& [Decision] is revise forms before runtime
  + [profile_0_2] adds a strict request form and a fourth observation_fault outcome
  + [observation_fault] carries a closed stage and closed local fault class without an OS error code or partial evidence
  + [open_and_query_fault] remain reserved for actual nonzero Win32 errors
  + [runtime] remains unauthorized until the revision is separately proven and a later unsafe source is processed

& [Nonclaim] is mandatory
  - never: cite this assessment as a successful Windows call, valid resource transfer, target-host fact, unsafe implementation authority, or scanner readiness
